% Test cases for the orthopedic footwear policy (orthopedic_footwear.le):
% synthetic claims, one or two per criterion of LCD L33641 and of Policy
% Article A52481, each stating only what its record shows. A shoe on a brace
% is an integral part of it; an insert or a heel is an accessory of its
% shoe. The queries: whether the claim is payable (the first query, so
% "stage" reads its checklist), whether it is reasonable and necessary, and
% what minimal change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base orthopedic_footwear cases includes these resources:
    orthopedic_footwear.

the knowledge base orthopedic_footwear cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete claim for an Oxford shoe (L3224) that is an integral part of a
% covered knee-ankle-foot orthosis (L2000): the order and the delivery.
scenario oxford_shoe_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the oxford shoe.
    the HCPCS code of the oxford shoe is "L3224".
    the oxford shoe is furnished to Ann.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the oxford shoe is an integral part of the KAFO.
    the HCPCS code of the KAFO is "L2000".
    the KAFO is a covered leg brace.
    the order for the oxford shoe is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the oxford shoe is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the oxford shoe includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the oxford shoe includes order date.
    the order for the oxford shoe includes description of the item.
    the order for the oxford shoe includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the oxford shoe includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the oxford shoe was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the oxford shoe was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the oxford shoe.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% A prosthetic shoe (L3250) holding the insert for a congenital absence of
% the foot and toes (Q72.31, group 1): reasonable and necessary, but the
% claim does not state the diagnosis code the Article requires.
scenario prosthetic_shoe_no_diagnosis_on_claim is:
    claim 1 is for the prosthetic shoe.
    the HCPCS code of the prosthetic shoe is "L3250".
    the prosthetic shoe is furnished to Ben.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the prosthetic shoe holds a removable custom fabricated insert for a partial foot amputation.
    the diagnosis code of Ben is "Q72.31".
    the order for the prosthetic shoe is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the prosthetic shoe is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the prosthetic shoe includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the prosthetic shoe includes order date.
    the order for the prosthetic shoe includes description of the item.
    the order for the prosthetic shoe includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the prosthetic shoe includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the prosthetic shoe was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the prosthetic shoe was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the prosthetic shoe.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: claim 1 states the diagnosis code of the beneficiary"]].

% Prosthetic shoes for other diagnoses: a diabetic foot ulcer (E11.621) is
% not a partial foot amputation.
scenario prosthetic_shoe_other_diagnosis is:
    claim 1 is for the prosthetic shoe.
    the HCPCS code of the prosthetic shoe is "L3250".
    the prosthetic shoe is furnished to Cy.
    the prosthetic shoe holds a removable custom fabricated insert for a partial foot amputation.
    the diagnosis code of Cy is "E11.621".
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% A partial foot amputation (S98.321A), but the shoe is put on over a
% partial foot prosthesis attached by other mechanisms (L5010): noncovered.
scenario shoe_over_prosthesis is:
    claim 1 is for the prosthetic shoe.
    the HCPCS code of the prosthetic shoe is "L3250".
    the prosthetic shoe is furnished to Dee.
    the prosthetic shoe holds a removable custom fabricated insert for a partial foot amputation.
    the prosthetic shoe is an integral part of the partial foot prosthesis.
    the HCPCS code of the partial foot prosthesis is "L5010".
    the diagnosis code of Dee is "S98.321A".
    rn expects answers [].

% Shoes not on a brace: an Oxford shoe (L3224) attached to nothing, a
% matching Oxford shoe (L3215) billed apart from the brace. Both statutorily
% excluded.
scenario shoes_not_on_a_brace is:
    claim 1 is for the oxford shoe.
    the HCPCS code of the oxford shoe is "L3224".
    the oxford shoe is furnished to Eve.
    claim 2 is for the matching shoe.
    the HCPCS code of the matching shoe is "L3215".
    the matching shoe is furnished to Eve.
    rn expects answers [].

% A high top shoe (L3649) on a covered AFO (L1990), an insert (L3000) and a
% heel replacement (L3455) on it: the shoe and the insert need the finding
% that they are necessary for the brace to function, the heel does not.
scenario high_top_shoe_on_brace is:
    claim 1 is for the high top shoe.
    the HCPCS code of the high top shoe is "L3649".
    the high top shoe is furnished to Fay.
    the high top shoe is an integral part of the AFO.
    the HCPCS code of the AFO is "L1990".
    the AFO is a covered leg brace.
    claim 2 is for the insert.
    the HCPCS code of the insert is "L3000".
    the insert is an accessory of the high top shoe.
    the insert is furnished to Fay.
    claim 3 is for the heel.
    the HCPCS code of the heel is "L3455".
    the heel is an accessory of the high top shoe.
    the heel is furnished to Fay.
    the finding footwear necessary for brace function about Fay is established, according to the orthotist, because "the AFO's stirrup is riveted to the shoe and needs a high top for ankle control".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 3 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A sole replacement (L3530) on a shoe of a covered brace, with no order:
% the Article needs none — payable.
scenario sole_replacement_without_order is:
    claim 1 is for the sole.
    the HCPCS code of the sole is "L3530".
    the sole is an accessory of the oxford shoe.
    the sole is furnished to Gus.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-05-01.
    the oxford shoe is an integral part of the KAFO.
    the HCPCS code of the KAFO is "L2020".
    the KAFO is a covered leg brace.
    the sole was delivered on 2026-05-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the sole.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].

% The Council finds the record does not show the high top shoe necessary for
% the brace to function; a foot pressure off-loading device (A9283) has no
% benefit at all.
scenario council_shoe_unsupported is:
    claim 1 is for the high top shoe.
    the HCPCS code of the high top shoe is "L3649".
    the high top shoe is furnished to Hal.
    the high top shoe is an integral part of the AFO.
    the HCPCS code of the AFO is "L1980".
    the AFO is a covered leg brace.
    the finding footwear necessary for brace function about Hal is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the brace is a plastic AFO worn inside any shoe; the record gives no reason it needs a high top".
    claim 2 is for the off-loading device.
    the HCPCS code of the off-loading device is "A9283".
    the off-loading device is furnished to Hal.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
